21. Architecture Review

This is an important part of an architect's job.

Application teams may come to me and say:

"We need to deploy this application on AWS."

I review their proposed architecture.

I ask:

Is it highly available?
Is the network secure?
Is the database appropriate?
Is there a single point of failure?
How will it scale?
What happens if an AZ fails?
What happens if the region fails?
How is data backed up?
How is access controlled?
How is it monitored?
What is the RTO/RPO?
What is the monthly cost?

Then I provide architectural recommendations.

